  "ingredients": [
    "16 ounce duck breast",
    "salt and pepper (to taste)",
    "2 tablespoon butter",
    "1 tablespoon stevia/erythritol blend (such as Swerve)",
    "1/4 teaspoon dried sage",
    "1/2 teaspoon orange extract",
    "1 tablespoon heavy whipping cream",
    "1 cup spinach"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Score the skin of the duck breast.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/orange-and-sage-glazed-duck-breast/#wprm-recipe-51503-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/img_9653.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Season on both sides with salt and pepper.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/orange-and-sage-glazed-duck-breast/#wprm-recipe-51503-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/img_9659.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Add the butter and sweetener to a pan over medium-low heat. Let cook until the butter is slightly browned.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/orange-and-sage-glazed-duck-breast/#wprm-recipe-51503-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/img_9664.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once the butter is a dark golden color, add the sage and orange extract. Let cook until the butter takes on a deep amber color.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/orange-and-sage-glazed-duck-breast/#wprm-recipe-51503-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/img_9667.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, place the duck breast in a cold pan, skin side down, on the stovetop. Turn the heat on to medium-high.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/orange-and-sage-glazed-duck-breast/#wprm-recipe-51503-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/img_9672.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "After a few minutes, flip the duck breast — the skin should be deliciously crisp.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/orange-and-sage-glazed-duck-breast/#wprm-recipe-51503-step-0-5",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/img_9679.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Stir the heavy cream into the orange and sage-infused butter. Pour the butter over the duck breast in the pan and let it mix with the duck fat. Cook for a few minutes longer. Once done, remove from the heat and rest for 2–3 minutes.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/orange-and-sage-glazed-duck-breast/#wprm-recipe-51503-step-0-6",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/img_9684.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Meanwhile, wilt the spinach in the pan used to make the sauce.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/orange-and-sage-glazed-duck-breast/#wprm-recipe-51503-step-0-7",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/img_9689.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Slice the duck and place it on top of the wilted spinach. Drizzle the sauce over and serve.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/orange-and-sage-glazed-duck-breast/#wprm-recipe-51503-step-0-8",
      "imageSource": null
    }
  ],
